<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="d0df9b4d">&lt;p&gt;
    The Release Burndown Chart displays all of the work planned for an entire release against the duration of the release
    and can be plotted via either a bar chart or a dual line graph. Both relay the amount of work left (vertical, Y
    axis)&amp;nbsp;in the release via either story point estimates or ideal days for any given sprint (horizontal, X axis).
    Actual work completed and the forecast for the upcoming sprints are both plotted to show actual progress and the view
    on the possible upcoming pace of delivery.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/examples/./resources/ReleaseBurndownChart_example.jpg&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;316&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/examples/./resources/ReleaseBurndownChart_example2.jpg&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;317&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
